course: dictionary
lesson: 971
title: Blur, the word that means unclear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blur is something you cannot see clearly, because it is moving fast or is out of focus. To blur is to make something unclear or smudgy. Look at the words around the word to find its meaning. «People who did not agree to be filmed have their faces blurred» tells you that blurring hides something, and the next part says why: adults and children have a right to privacy.
explain: The context can also show you a meaning you might not expect. «Tell me about volcanoes» gets a blur, but «Explain in five steps why volcanoes erupt, for a 9-year-old» gets something useful. A blur here is a vague answer that is not clear enough to use. Try the meaning in the sentence: a vague, unclear answer still makes sense.
explain: Blur also has a verb form, used in «blurred vision» and «blur the line between». Blurred vision means you cannot see clearly. To blur the line between two things means to make the difference between them less clear. Blur, blurs, blurred and blurring all come from the same idea of unclear.
fact: Blur can be a noun (a blur) or a verb (to blur).
fact: A blur is something you cannot see clearly because it is moving fast or out of focus.
fact: To blur something is to make it unclear or smudgy.
fact: «Blurred vision» is one sign of concussion, a knock to the head.
fact: «Blur the line between» means to make a difference less clear.
exercise: «People who did not agree to be filmed have their faces blurred.» Why are their faces blurred? | *To keep who they are private | To make the film louder | To show they are happy | To make them look more beautiful
exercise: Phone cameras can «blur backgrounds». What does this do? | *Makes the background unclear so the person stands out | Makes the photo louder | Turns the photo black and white | Makes the person disappear
exercise: «Signs of concussion include headache, dizziness, feeling sick, blurred vision, confusion.» Find and copy one word that means not clear. | dizziness | *blurred | confusion | headache
test: «Tell me about volcanoes» gets a blur. What does a blur mean here? | A picture of a volcano | A clear, detailed answer | *A vague answer that is not clear enough to use | A question about volcanoes
test: What does «blur the line between» mean? | Make the line very bright | Draw a straight line | *Make the difference between two things less clear | Rub out a line
exam: Which word means the same as «blurred» in «blurred vision»? | Bright | *Unclear | Loud | Clear
